 "answer_text": "Found 1 gene record for Huntington disease: huntingtin [2]. \n\nHuntington disease is a monogenic neurodegenerative disorder showing autosomal-dominant inheritance, and the causative genetic mutation was identified in 1993 [1]. The principles of genetic testing are explained in published reviews of the disease [1]. \n\nGene records found\n\nGene NCBIGene:3064, name: huntingtin [2]. \n\nPubmed records found\n\nPubmed title: Huntington disease [3]. Pubmed title: Huntington disease [20]. Pubmed title: Huntington disease [22]. Pubmed title: Huntington disease: When does it begin [24]. Pubmed title: What Is Huntington Disease [26]. \n\nMedgen records found\n\nMedgen title: Huntington disease [4]. \n\nClinical features MedGen lists for Huntington disease\n\nMedgen clinical_features: Chorea [5]. Medgen clinical_features: Depression [6]. Medgen clinical_features: Gliosis [7]. Medgen clinical_features: Rigidity [8]. Medgen clinical_features: Seizure [9]. Medgen clinical_features: Hyperreflexia [10]. Medgen clinical_features: Bradykinesia [11]. Medgen clinical_features: Personality changes [12]. Medgen clinical_features: Abnormality of eye movement [13]. Medgen clinical_features: Dementia [14]. Medgen clinical_features: Cerebellar atrophy [15]. Medgen clinical_features: Gait ataxia [16]. Medgen clinical_features: Neuronal loss in central nervous system [17]. \n\nLiterature entity records found\n\nLiterature entity name: Huntington Disease [18]. \n\nClinical trial records found\n\nClinical trial name: Prospective Huntington At Risk Observational Study [19]. Clinical trial name: Family Health After Predictive Huntington Disease (HD) Testing [21]. Clinical trial name: Bioavailability of Ubiquinol in Huntington Disease [23]. Clinical trial name: Study of Huntington Patients in Connection With European Huntington's Disease Network (EHDN) [25]. Clinical trial name: Resveratrol and Huntington Disease [27]. "
